            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0093" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/549</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Russia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-12T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1308. Department has received information from several sources that the
                    Socialists of Germany and Russia are preparing to hold a meeting for the purpose
                    of discussing possible terms of peace. Such reports are disturbing, as a
                    separate peace would make impossible any assistance for Russia, financial or
                    otherwise, from this country. Carefully and discreetly investigate and report
                    immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
